<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/character.css" asp-append-version="true" />
<section class="characters" data-characters lang="zh-Hans">
    <header class="character-intro">
        <a class="character-back" href="/Archeon"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">← 回到 Archeon</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>← Back to Archeon</span></a>
        <p class="kd-eyebrow" lang="en">06 · Character</p>
        <h1><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">在风与日光里</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>In wind and sunlight</span></h1>
        <p class="character-lede"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Anna、Lia 与 Kassia。启程之前，先在她们身边坐一会儿。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Anna, Lia and Kassia. Before the next departure, sit with them a while.</span></p>
    </header>
    <div class="character-toolbar" data-character-toolbar>
        <nav class="character-jumps" aria-label="人物 / Characters">
            <a href="#anna" lang="en">Anna <span>01</span></a>
            <a href="#lia" lang="en">Lia <span>02</span></a>
            <a href="#kassia" lang="en">Kassia <span>03</span></a>
        </nav>
        <div class="character-language" data-language-controls role="group" aria-label="阅读语言 / Reading language" hidden>
            <button type="button" data-character-lang="zh" aria-pressed="true" lang="zh-Hans">中文</button>
            <button type="button" data-character-lang="en" aria-pressed="false" lang="en">English</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="character-time"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">年龄以主线开始时为准，身高与体重为约值。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Ages are given at the start of the main story; height and weight are approximate.</span></p>

    <article id="anna" class="character-profile" aria-labelledby="anna-name">
        <figure class="character-portrait">
            <img src="/images/Anna%20Freedman-protagonist.png" width="1568" height="1407" alt="Anna 穿着红夹克，金色长发在船下的日光里扬起。" data-alt-zh="Anna 穿着红夹克，金色长发在船下的日光里扬起。" data-alt-en="Anna in her red jacket, long blonde hair lifting in the sunlight beneath a ship." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption><span>01</span> Anna Freedman</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="character-copy">
            <header data-reading-anchor>
                <p class="character-place"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Atheria · 鹰巢</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Atheria · Eyrie</span></p>
                <h2 id="anna-name" lang="en">Anna Freedman</h2>
                <p class="character-craft"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Gust · 飞行与制作</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Gust · Flying &amp; making</span></p>
            </header>
            <dl class="character-facts" data-reading-anchor>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">年龄</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Age</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">19 岁</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>19</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">身高</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Height</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 168 cm</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 168 cm</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">体重</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Weight</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 58 kg</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 58 kg</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">头发</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Hair</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">金色长发</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Long blonde hair</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">眼睛</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Eyes</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">蓝灰色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Blue-grey</span></dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div class="character-prose">
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Anna 倾听时会微微侧过头，金色长发从肩边滑下来，露出红夹克里一截白领。她的声音偏低，说得快，字却清楚；一讲到兴头上，手里拿着的小铜件也跟着转。夹克合身，肩上的金边是她自己挑的。她喜欢隔着一段泊位就能看见的红，也在意抬起胳膊时，袖子会不会牵住肩。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Anna tips her head when she listens. Blonde hair slips from her shoulder, uncovering a little of the white collar inside her red jacket. Her voice is low and quick, the words distinct; once she warms to a story, the small brass fitting in her hand turns with every gesture. The jacket fits her well. She chose the gold edging at the shoulders herself. She likes a red you can pick out across the moorings, and she cares whether a sleeve pulls when she lifts her arm.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Gust 的栗色甲板在日光里慢慢变暖，脚下有燃料电池持续的低鸣。Anna 站得稳，目光却常往舷边去：风布刚抬起来，哪根细索的响已经变了。她会把听见的位置指给同行的人，也会蹲下来，为一只握着硌手的柄重新磨出弧度。皮手套沾着油，飞行包侧袋里那半瓶山花油，开盖时仍有一点清淡的香。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>The chestnut-coloured deck of Gust warms slowly in the sun. Beneath it, the fuel cell holds a steady hum. Anna stands firmly, her attention travelling to the rail: a strip of windcloth has only just lifted, but which slender line has already changed its note? She points out the place for someone else to hear. Then she might crouch over an uncomfortable handle, sanding its curve until it sits better in the hand. Her leather gloves carry oil; the half-bottle of wildflower oil in her flight bag still releases a faint fragrance when opened.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">回到 Atheria，她有时还没把包放稳，就开始向母亲讲路上的事。讲得太急，漏掉一个人名，被追问了又只好退回去重说。她爱远行，也爱把某个下午讲得让桌边的人忍不住插话；笑起来可以毫无顾忌，争起一处做法也不肯轻易让步。第二天摊开材料，她还记得昨天那个没来得及试的小念头。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Back in Atheria, she sometimes starts telling her mother about the journey before she has set her bag down properly. In her hurry she leaves out a name, gets interrupted, and has to go back. She loves travelling, and loves recounting an afternoon until everyone at the table has something to add. She laughs freely and argues a way of making something with equal enthusiasm. When she lays out her materials the next morning, she still remembers the little idea she never got round to trying yesterday.</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>

    <article id="lia" class="character-profile" aria-labelledby="lia-name">
        <figure class="character-portrait">
            <img src="/images/Lia%20redwood.png" width="819" height="1452" alt="Lia 扎起长发，在日光照亮的木屋与草地之间回过头来。" data-alt-zh="Lia 扎起长发，在日光照亮的木屋与草地之间回过头来。" data-alt-en="Lia, her long hair tied up, turning among sunlit timber houses and grass." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption><span>02</span> Lia Redwood</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="character-copy">
            <header data-reading-anchor>
                <p class="character-place"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Atheria</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Atheria</span></p>
                <h2 id="lia-name" lang="en">Lia Redwood</h2>
                <p class="character-craft"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">颜色、织面与精细小件</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Colour, cloth &amp; small mechanisms</span></p>
            </header>
            <dl class="character-facts" data-reading-anchor>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">年龄</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Age</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">14 岁</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>14</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">身高</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Height</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 149 cm</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 149 cm</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">体重</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Weight</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 44 kg</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 44 kg</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">头发</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Hair</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">红棕色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Auburn</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">眼睛</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Eyes</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">浅绿色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Pale green</span></dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div class="character-prose">
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Lia 会把样布拿到门口再看。屋里的颜色到了太阳下，边缘往往另有一点亮；她捏住两角，让织面平展开，红棕色的发丝垂到脸旁，浅绿色的眼睛还追着那一小块差别。旁边的人已经说了好看，她却要等湿气散些再答。若一道接缝留得太毛，吃饭时她也可能想起来，再抱怨一句。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Lia takes the cloth sample to the doorway for another look. A colour seen indoors often has a different brightness along its edge in sunlight. She holds two corners and spreads the weave flat, auburn strands falling beside her face, her pale-green eyes following that small difference. Someone has already called it beautiful. She wants to let it dry a little before answering. If a seam has been left too rough, she may remember it over a meal and complain all over again.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">小扣件在指间闭合，轻轻一嗒，她会重新开一次，试那一点阻力。簧片回得是否齐整，绷紧的细线有没有把一边拉歪，都是她肯花时间看的东西。碰到没学过的结构，她就拿给熟悉它的人看，问清楚，再试。专心时她可以盯很久，旁边一笔画歪了，也足够让她笑得暂时放下手里的东西。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>A small clasp closes between her fingers with a soft click. She opens it once more to feel the resistance. Whether a spring returns evenly, whether a taut thread has pulled one edge crooked: these are things she will spend time looking at. An unfamiliar mechanism goes to someone who knows it; she asks, listens, and tries again. She can concentrate for a long while, yet a drawing gone lopsided beside her is enough to make her put everything down and laugh.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Anna 讲起远方，Lia 常在她以为已经讲完的地方接着问：风究竟从哪边来，人在地上还能不能认出空中的那座山。她想自己去看，也会记得一顿不好吃的饭，和一个值得再坐一会儿的地方。碗底还剩一点甜，她明明说饱了，勺子却又刮过去；听见朋友取笑，就抬起眼，把刚才没争完的话接下去。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>When Anna talks about somewhere far away, Lia often begins her questions just where Anna thought the story had finished. Which way did the wind come from? Could you still recognise that mountain once you were on the ground? She wants to go and see. She will remember a disappointing meal, too, and a place worth sitting in a little longer. There is something sweet left at the bottom of her bowl. She has said she is full, but her spoon scrapes across it again; when a friend teases her, she looks up and takes their unfinished argument straight back up.</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>

    <article id="kassia" class="character-profile" aria-labelledby="kassia-name">
        <figure class="character-portrait">
            <img src="/images/kassia.png" width="785" height="1484" alt="Kassia 头顶黄铜色护目镜，发丝与肩边的布料被田野上的风吹起。" data-alt-zh="Kassia 头顶黄铜色护目镜，发丝与肩边的布料被田野上的风吹起。" data-alt-en="Kassia with brass-coloured goggles above her brow, hair and shoulder cloth lifting in the wind over the fields." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption><span>03</span> Kassia Ashcroft</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="character-copy">
            <header data-reading-anchor>
                <p class="character-place"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">常在各处航路交汇地停留</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Often found where routes meet</span></p>
                <h2 id="kassia-name" lang="en">Kassia Ashcroft</h2>
                <p class="character-craft"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Razor · 飞行</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Razor · Flying</span></p>
            </header>
            <dl class="character-facts" data-reading-anchor>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">年龄</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Age</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">21 岁</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>21</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">身高</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Height</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 172 cm</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 172 cm</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">体重</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Weight</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 60 kg</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 60 kg</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">头发</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Hair</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">棕色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Brown</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">眼睛</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Eyes</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">棕色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Brown</span></dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div class="character-prose">
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">风把 Kassia 的发丝吹到眼前，她抬手拨开，护目镜的铜色边框在额上闪了一下。棕色的眼睛从高处风布移到泊位，又回来看人。她喜欢让 Razor 的进场利落又漂亮，小艇的电机声比 Gust 更尖；落稳以后，若有人看见刚才那一下，她脸上的得意也用不着藏。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Wind blows Kassia’s hair across her eyes. She brushes it aside, and the brass-coloured rim of her goggles catches the light above her brow. Her brown eyes move from the high windcloth to the mooring, then back to the person beside her. She likes to bring Razor in neatly, with a little grace; the skiff’s motor has a sharper note than Gust’s. Once she is down, if someone noticed that last manoeuvre, she sees no reason to hide her pleasure.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Anna 说风要变，她会问是哪一根索先响，站在哪里能听清。纸上的字挤了，她嫌别人写得难读；有人说她自己的字更小，她便抽过来，念得又快又清楚，念完还要问谁没听见。她记得一个判断怎样来的，也记得朋友哪回看错了。争论能从风牌边一直带到饭桌，两个人刚为航向争过，又开始争碗里究竟是太甜还是太淡。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>When Anna says the wind is about to change, Kassia asks which line sounded different first, and where she should stand to hear it. She complains when someone has crowded their writing onto a sheet. Told that her own is smaller, she takes the paper and reads it aloud, quickly and clearly, then asks who missed a word. She remembers how a judgement was reached, and which time a friend got it wrong. An argument can follow them from the wind board to the table: having disputed a heading, they begin on whether the food is too sweet or too bland.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">她有自己的船、朋友和下一段去向。有时 Anna 到，她已经提起包要走；有时一顿饭吃完，她还愿意坐着，听对方把话补齐。她的玩笑可能刺人，手却照样把另一碗推过去，催人趁热吃。甜食拿少了，她会再回去一趟，回来也不肯承认刚才分得太快。谁若先笑她，往往得准备好被回敬一句。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>She has her own ship, her own friends, and somewhere else to go. Sometimes Anna arrives just as she is picking up her bag. Sometimes the meal is over and she is still happy to sit, letting Anna finish what she was saying. A joke of hers may sting; she will still push the other bowl across and tell you to eat while it is hot. If she took too little of something sweet, she goes back for more. On returning, she refuses to admit she handed it round too quickly. Whoever laughs first had better have an answer ready.</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>
